  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Evaluate $\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta+3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1$.\n\nSet $a=\\sin^2\\theta$ and $b=\\cos^2\\theta$, so $a+b=1$, and factor $a^3+b^3$.",
      "worked": "Let $a=\\sin^2\\theta$ and $b=\\cos^2\\theta$. Then $a+b=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta+3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta&=a^3+b^3+3ab\\\\\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta+3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta&=(a+b)(a^2-ab+b^2)+3ab\\\\\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta+3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta&=a^2+2ab+b^2\\\\\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta+3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta&=(a+b)^2\\\\\\sin^6\\theta+\\cos^6\\theta+3\\sin^2\\theta\\cos^2\\theta&=1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 45
  },
